    turnFlow: "Dealer stakes the board (Pope, Matrimony, Intrigue, Ace, King, Queen, Jack, Game). Fifty-one cards are dealt evenly to players plus one face-down stop hand; the last card of the stop hand is turned for trump. Eldest leads by playing a card face up (any suit, must be lowest held). Players continue the ascending sequence in that suit until a stop (King, 7 of Diamonds, or card whose successor is in the stop hand). The player who played the stop leads the next sequence with lowest card of any suit. The 9 of Diamonds (Pope) acts as any card. Compartments are won by playing the matching trump card or, for Game, by being first to empty one's hand. First out wins the Game stake and receives one counter per card from each opponent (holder of the Pope is excused).",
